    "description": "Wolf Trail 🇵🇱🇩🇪🇨🇭🇦🇹🇸🇮🇮🇹 Europe’s newest thru-hiking trail | 3493 km ~ 2170 miles | 4-6 months | info 👇\n\nThe Wolf Trail is a new thru-hike that goes coast-to-coast from northern Poland to Trieste on the Adriatic Sea in Italy. It stitches together existing premier routes including the E9 (Coastal Path), E1, Nord–Süd Route, and the Via Alpina into one seamless odyssey. It crosses six countries through forests, countryside, mountains, and the Mediterranean. We’re very stoked to launch this new thru-hiking trail 🤩\n\nIf you don’t have the time to hike the full Wolf Trail, no worries, you can also very easily section-hike it 🙏\n \nAll stages👇\n\n1️⃣ Baltic Start, 428 km | 266 mi\n2️⃣ Rivers & Plains, 543 km | 337.5 mi\n3️⃣ The Green Heart, 487 km | 302 mi\n4️⃣ Forests & Wine, 583 km | 362 mi\n5️⃣ High Watch, 581 km | 361 mi\n6️⃣ Alpine Gateway, 394 km | 245 mi\n7️⃣ Alpine Crossing, 591 km | 367 mi\n\nFrom the end of April, you can follow these amazing hikers on their journey, setting off in Poland and ending in Trieste:\n\n🔹 @laurenroerick\n🔸 @timothyvslarsen\n🔹 @elinasborne\n🔸 @marc_is_walking\n\nMore info, the GPX, and everything else coming soon. Make sure you follow @jackwolfskin and @_thru_hiking for the latest updates! \n\nSee you on the trails! 💚\n\n📍 Wolf Trail\n🏃‍♂️ Thru-hike\n🥾 3493 km / 2170 miles\n📅 4 to 6 months\n⛰️ Hills, urban, forest, mountains, countryside\n.\n.\n.\n.\n#thruhiking #wolftrail #thruhike",
